        setup: {
          players: '4 players in two fixed partnerships (North-South vs East-West).',
          deck: '33 cards: A, K, O, U, 10, 9, 8, 7 in four suits plus the WELI (6 of Bells).',
          equipment: 'German-suited deck, score pad.',
          dealing: 'Deal 5 cards to each player. Forehand shows a card rank (Schlag) to the dealer in secret; the dealer shows a suit back to forehand in secret.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win at least three out of five tricks to win the hand. First team to 15 or 18 points wins the match.',
          gameplay: "1. **Secret Selection**: Forehand and dealer establish rank and suit trumps in secret. 2. **Play**: Forehand leads. **Must Follow Suit** only applies to forehand and dealer for trumps. Partners have no follow obligation but must try to deduce trumps. 3. **The Cards**: Highest card is the 'Guate' (Schlag + 1), followed by the 'Rechte' (Schlag in trump suit), then the 'Linken' (Schlag in the other suit of same color).",
          keyRules: [
            'No signals or verbal communication allowed between partners.',
            "The first trick's cards remain face up on the table to assist in deduction.",
            'WELI is always bells unless 6 is the Schlag.',
            'Betting (raising the stakes) can be done at any time during the hand.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'As the player who knows the trump, use your first play to signal clearly to your partner. If you lead a trump, your partner will likely identify the suit immediately.',
          intermediate: 'Deduction: If your partner (who knows trumps) plays a card and the dealer is forced to follow with a trump, you now know the trump suit. Use this knowledge to support the next lead.',
          advanced: "The False Signal: Occasionally play a non-trump high card to see if opponents take the bait and assume it's trumps, potentially leading them to waste their own high cards.",
          tips: [
            'Watch the face-up first trick throughout the game.',
            "Don't raise the stakes until you are reasonably certain your partner has identified the trumps.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        variations: {
          list: [
