          deckDescription: 'One standard 32-card pack plus the Weli (joker-like card): eight ranks (seven through ace) in each of four German suits, plus one permanent trump (Weli). Used for Blind Watten where the Schlag (called rank) determines the four top trumps and the Weli is always the highest.',
          suitDescription: 'Four German suits (hearts, leaves, bells, acorns). Each suit has eight cards; the Weli is a separate card that always counts as trump. The Schlag (ace, ten, king, queen, or jack) determines which four cards are the top trumps for the round.',
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit plus Weli. The called Schlag rank yields four top trumps (Guate, Rechte, Linken, and the fourth of that rank). Weli is highest; then the four Schlag trumps in order; then the rest by Watten rules.',
          dealPattern: 'Cards are dealt in one round of five cards each.',
          bettingLimits: 'None',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'None; card rank comparison determines trick wins (varies by secret Schlag).',
          rankingSystem: 'Watten (Guate-Rechte-Linken)',
          useTrump: true,
